{
  "_about": [
    "The Dungeon Journal's bosses, kept by hand; Tools/build/journal.py turns this into one Lua",
    "file per dungeon in NaowhForever_DungeonJournal/Data/Dungeons. Dungeons in level order, named as the",
    "client and NaowhForever_DungeonJournal/Data/Quests.lua name them. Each wing lists its bosses in kill order,",
    "named as Wowhead Forever names the NPC; npcs pins an ID where the name is ambiguous. A",
    "boss listed under rare is optional and may not spawn. zone is the Wowhead zone, guide a",
    "Wowhead guide with a Loot tab per boss for dungeons whose bosses have no drop data yet.",
    "entranceZone is the Wowhead zone the entrance is in, for its territory. entrance is where",
    "it is on Forever's map (uiMapID, x, y) and where that came from; left out where no source",
    "matches Forever's map, for the game to learn. encounterNames gives a boss's name in the",
    "game's DungeonEncounter table where it differs from ours, so the build finds its encounter",
    "ID (what ENCOUNTER_END names it by, for the kill count). Magmatus (Infurnus) and The Baron",
    "(The Butcher) are matched by elimination, the only encounter left in their place: unproven.",
    "Arcanic Enigma is Dalaran's Mana Elemental encounter: its quest says slay the Mana Elemental,",
    "and no Forever NPC of that name is in Dalaran. Also unproven.",
    "new marks a dungeon that is new in WoW Forever, not in the classic game. A raid has raid",
    "(its size) and announced: only a raid announced for Forever is built; loot false leaves its",
    "loot out until Wowhead has Forever drops for it. note is shown at the",
    "top of its page; encounterIDs pins encounter IDs the game's table does not show yet.",
    "add places items on a boss by hand, { \"Boss Name\": [item IDs] }: Forever drops players have",
    "seen that Wowhead has not tied to the boss yet (the game's tables cannot say who drops an",
    "item). The build watcher's report lists the new gear each build adds, to place here.",
 "countedWith names the boss whose fight a boss with none falls in (Sneed's Shredder, which",
 "Sneed climbs out of): its kills count with that fight's, as the game reports no other way.",
    "wowsrc is the dungeon's wowsrc.com loot page (its slug, or { wing: slug }), read by",
    "Tools/sources/wowsrc.py: Forever's own list of each boss's drops and its trash's, which the build",
    "adds to Wowhead's (wowsrcNames maps a boss name of theirs to ours where they differ).",
    "optional lists a wing's bosses a run can skip (an event, a summon, an optional fight):",
    "unnumbered, like a rare. chests lists its loot chests by Wowhead object ID: what each",
    "holds comes from Wowhead's object page (Classic's where Forever's is empty) and wowsrc."
  ],
